From: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: realtek-otto: add RTL8197F support

The RTL8197F router SoC has the GPIO block the Otto switch SoCs derive
from: two banks of four 8-bit ports (A-D at 0x3500, E-H at 0x351c) with
the same CNR, DIR, DATA, ISR and IMR registers. The CPU runs little
endian and port A is held in the least significant byte, with two IMR
bits per line starting at bit 0. This matches the reversed port order
handling of the driver, so reuse it.

Signed-off-by: Roman Rikhter <teledurak@gmail.com>
---
Index: linux-6.18.52/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/realtek,otto-gpio.yaml
===================================================================
--- linux-6.18.52.orig/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/realtek,otto-gpio.yaml
+++ linux-6.18.52/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpio/realtek,otto-gpio.yaml
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@ properties:
   compatible:
     items:
       - enum:
+          - realtek,rtl8197f-gpio
           - realtek,rtl8380-gpio
           - realtek,rtl8390-gpio
           - realtek,rtl9300-gpio
Index: linux-6.18.52/drivers/gpio/gpio-realtek-otto.c
===================================================================
--- linux-6.18.52.orig/drivers/gpio/gpio-realtek-otto.c
+++ linux-6.18.52/drivers/gpio/gpio-realtek-otto.c
@@ -339,6 +339,10 @@ static const struct of_device_id realtek
 		.data = (void *)GPIO_INTERRUPTS_DISABLED,
 	},
 	{
+		.compatible = "realtek,rtl8197f-gpio",
+		.data = (void *)GPIO_PORTS_REVERSED,
+	},
+	{
 		.compatible = "realtek,rtl8380-gpio",
 	},
 	{
